PROJECT STRUCTURE AND ARCHITECTURE MAP
======================================

Project: Transient_Diffusion1D_FDM_Solvers_Cpp
Domain: One-dimensional transient diffusion equation solved with finite-difference methods.
Language: C++20.
Build system: CMake 3.20 or newer.
Primary include convention: project-root-relative paths, for example
  #include "Core/Field/Field.hpp"

PURPOSE OF THIS FILE
--------------------
This file is an AI-oriented architecture map. It describes the current source tree,
module responsibilities, target dependencies, data flow, numerical schemes, and important
implementation contracts. It intentionally does not rely on README files.

Notation:
- .hpp files declare interfaces, data structures, inline utilities, and header-only code.
- .cpp files contain out-of-line implementations and are compiled by CMake.
- [entry point] identifies a translation unit containing main().
- Generated build directories, binaries, plots, and large result snapshots are summarized.
- The project root is the include directory for every CMake target.

