CONFIGURED NUMERICAL MODEL
--------------------------
The current values in Config/SolverInputs.hpp define:
- Domain length: SolverInputs::Geometry::Length.
- Diffusivity/kinematic viscosity: SolverInputs::Physics::nu.
- Uniform mesh node count: SolverInputs::Mesh::N.
- Number of time levels, requested dt, and convergence tolerance:
  SolverInputs::Solver::NumTimeLevels, dt, and Tolerance.
- Initial profile: SolverInputs::InitialCondition::Profile.
- Fixed top and bottom values: SolverInputs::BoundaryCondition::TopWallValue and BottomWallValue.

Geometry validates positive length. Mesh uses N nodes and computes the spacing as
Delta = Length / (N - 1). Field objects are sized from the mesh and store nodal scalar
values. In this one-dimensional project, Boundary orientation is represented by the
Horizontal/Vertical enum and location identifies Left/Right/Bottom/Top; the active
simulation setup creates vertical top and bottom Dirichlet boundaries.

ARCHITECTURAL RESPONSIBILITIES
------------------------------
1. Config
   Owns centralized physical, mesh, initial-condition, boundary, and solver inputs.

2. Core
   Provides domain geometry, uniform mesh coordinates, boundary metadata, and nodal fields.
   Core is the foundation used by discretization, setup, verification, IO, and solvers.

3. SimulationSetup
   Builds the shared simulation state. SimulationContext owns Geometry, Mesh,
   SimulationParams, SimulationBoundaries, Plot, and the working fields U_0, U_1,
   U_nMinus1, U_n, U_nPlus1, U_SteadyState, and U_Analytical_n.

4. Discretization
   Contains time-marching schemes. Explicit schemes update fields directly. Implicit
   schemes assemble dense or tridiagonal systems and use boundary enforcement before solving.
   FTCS stability requires diffusion number <= 0.5; FTCS_Stability.hpp can reduce dt and
   update the diffusion number when the requested value is unstable.

5. LinearSolvers
   Provides matrix/vector storage plus Gaussian elimination and Thomas algorithm solvers.
   Gaussian elimination consumes CoefficientMatrix and RHS. ThomasAlgorithm consumes
   TridiagonalMatrix and RHS. Matrix constructors are out-of-line in their own .cpp files.

6. Utilities
   Supplies reusable parameter, convergence, time-scale, status, and keyboard helpers.

7. Verification
   Computes analytical steady/transient diffusion fields for comparison against numerical
   fields. AnalyticalSolution functions write into an existing Field object.

8. IO
   Writes field data under Results/, builds output names and paths, and provides gnuplot
   plotting through LinePlot and LivePointPlotter.

9. main
   Each executable selects one SolverScheme, creates SimulationContext, performs any
   scheme-specific setup, advances time levels, calls common post-processing, and exits.

SIMULATION DATA FLOW
--------------------
SolverInputs -> Geometry -> Mesh -> SimulationParams and Field objects
             -> SimulationBoundaries and Plot dashboard
             -> selected discretization scheme
             -> optional matrix/RHS assembly and LinearSolvers
             -> boundary application and relative-field-change calculation
             -> SimulationContext output/plotting and analytical comparison
             -> Results/Initial_Field, Results/Numerical_Field, Results/Analytical_Field

FIELD STATE CONVENTION
----------------------
- U_0 is the initial field.
- For one-step schemes, StartUp moves the initial state into U_n.
- U_nPlus1 is the newly computed field before common post-processing swaps it into U_n.
- DuFort-Frankel additionally uses U_nMinus1 and its two-level update.
- SimulationContext applies configured boundary values, computes relative field change,
  updates fields, writes periodic output, updates plots, and checks steady-state tolerance.

CMAKE TARGET ARCHITECTURE
-------------------------
CMake uses C++20, project-root include directories, -Wall -Wextra -O3 on GCC/Clang,
and enables IPO/LTO only when check_ipo_supported() succeeds. Runtime executables are
written to ${CMAKE_SOURCE_DIR}/bin and compile_commands.json is exported.

Static libraries:
- cfd_core
  Sources: Core/Boundary, Core/Geometry, Core/Mesh, Core/Field implementations.

- cfd_explicit
  Sources: FTCS.cpp and DuFortFrankel.cpp.
  Public dependency: cfd_core.

- cfd_linear_solvers
  Sources: GaussianElimination.cpp, ThomasAlgorithm.cpp, and the three matrix .cpp files.
  Public dependency: cfd_core.

- cfd_implicit
  Sources: EnforceBoundary.cpp, CrankNicolsonAssembler.cpp, LaasonenAssembler.cpp.
  Public dependencies: cfd_core and cfd_linear_solvers.

- cfd_io
  Sources: FileWriter.cpp, LivePointPlotter.cpp, LinePlot.cpp.
  Public dependency: cfd_core.

- cfd_utilities
  Source: FieldChange.cpp.
  Public dependency: cfd_core.

- cfd_verification
  Source: AnalyticalSolution.cpp.
  Public dependency: cfd_core.

- cfd_simulation_setup
  Sources: Plot.cpp, SimulationBoundaries.cpp, SimulationContext.cpp, SimulationParams.cpp.
  Public dependencies: cfd_core, cfd_io, cfd_utilities, cfd_verification.

- cfd_all_libraries
  Aggregate custom target depending on every static library above. It builds libraries only,
  without requesting the executable targets.

Executable targets:
- Explicit_FTCS -> cfd_explicit, cfd_simulation_setup
- Explicit_DUFORT_FRANKEL -> cfd_explicit, cfd_simulation_setup
- Implicit_Laasonen -> cfd_implicit, cfd_linear_solvers, cfd_simulation_setup
- Implicit_CrankNicolson -> cfd_implicit, cfd_linear_solvers, cfd_simulation_setup

BUILD COMMANDS
--------------
Configure:
  cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release

Build all configured targets:
  cmake --build build --parallel

Build libraries only:
  cmake --build build --target cfd_all_libraries --parallel

Build one executable:
  cmake --build build --target Explicit_FTCS
  cmake --build build --target Explicit_DUFORT_FRANKEL
  cmake --build build --target Implicit_Laasonen
  cmake --build build --target Implicit_CrankNicolson

IMPORTANT MAINTENANCE RULES FOR AN AI AGENT
-------------------------------------------
- Treat CMakeLists.txt as the authoritative source list and target dependency map.
- Do not reintroduce old paths such as LinearSolvers/Matrix/RHS.hpp; matrix headers now
  live in their own directories: Matrix/RHS/RHS.hpp, Matrix/CoefficientMatrix/CoefficientMatrix.hpp,
  and Matrix/TridiagonalMatrix/TridiagonalMatrix.hpp.
- The line-plot class is LinePlot and its current files are under IO/Visualization/gnuplot/LinePlot/.
- The plot dashboard is under SimulationSetup/PostProcessing/PlotDashboard/Plot/.
- Keep header-only utilities out of CMake source lists unless they are intentionally compiled.
- Preserve the distinction between generated Results data and source code.
- Before editing, inspect git status and preserve unrelated user changes.
